      inspect: true

    p.Article-Paragraph.
      There are the following #[+Keyword--YDID anomalies]:

    ul.Article-UnorderedList

      li The #[+SecondaryEntity__Code--YDID p(sample4)] has been #[+Keyword--YDID ignored].

      li.
        The #[+SecondaryEntity__Code--YDID typeof(sample4) == "null"] is #[+Keyword--YDID truthy] but
          #[+SecondaryEntity__Code--YDID sample4 == null] is #[+Keyword--YDID falsy].

    p.Article-Paragraph.
      From above experiments we can conclude that the direct comparison with #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID null] is
        #[+Keyword--YDID unsafe].
      #[+Keyword__Contrast--YDID Instead], the #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID typeof(x) == "null] or
        #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID typeof(x) == "null] comparisons should be used, but
        #[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID isNull]/#[+ImportantEntity__Code--YDID isNotNull] #[+Term--YDID functions]
        suggested by #[+ImportantEntity--YDID YDF] are the #[+Keyword--YDID shorter]
        #[+Keyword__Contrast--YDID alternatives].


    //- ╍╍╍ `isNotNull`╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍╍
